-- title:
--   Scalar re-alignment of a Frobenius twist in Čerednik–Drinfeld descent
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ assumed to be a discrete valuation ring, with an irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$; let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (written `Onr`) be a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo it, every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo it, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo it. Let $\mathrm{vdet}:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (multiplicatively written) satisfy $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$. Let $R_1$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$, $\iota_0$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map of that quaternion algebra into $M_2(K_0)$, $v$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$, and $\tilde\Gamma$ a subgroup of the quaternion units whose members are exactly those of `awayUnits R₁ v`, i.e. the intersection over all primes $w\neq v$ of the preimages, under the localisation map at $w$, of the subgroups generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$. Let $G$ be a finite group, $\theta:\tilde\Gamma\to G$ a homomorphism, $k$ an algebraically closed $\mathcal O$-algebra field, $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma\times G$ and $\psi:\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map. Assume: for every $y$ fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0(z))}$ for all scalar elements $z=c_0\cdot 1$ of $\tilde\Gamma$ with $\theta(z)=1$, one has $\psi(y)=\psi(\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0(\gamma_1))}y)$. Then there is $z=(z_1,z_2)\in\tilde\Gamma\times G$ with $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0(z_1\gamma_1))}=\psi$, and such that for every pair $x=(x_1,x_2)$ consisting of a Deligne datum $x_1$ over $k$ (for $K_0$, $\pi$) and an element $x_2\in G$: $x_1$ is its own pullback along $\iota_0(z_1)^{-1}$, that is, for every full lattice $M$ the line of $x_1$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $x_1$ at $\iota_0(z_1)^{-1}M$ under the base-changed action map, and $x_2=\theta(z_1)\,x_2\,z_2^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the re-alignment (lifting) hypothesis needed to run the fibre-descent step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld $r$-adic uniformisation of a quaternionic Shimura curve: a Frobenius twist of a coefficient map that is already trivial on the subring fixed by the scalars of $\tilde\Gamma$ in the kernel of the level character can be undone by multiplying $\gamma$ by an element acting trivially on the Deligne-datum functor and adjusting the $G$-component. It is used in the proof of the coarse-moduli uniformisation statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsCoarseModuli.exists_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_of_span_eq_of_geometricallyConnected_of_squarefree_of_isUnit_two_of_geometricallyConnected_tower_of_isUnit_three`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsCoarseModuli.exists_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_of_span_eq_of_geometricallyConnected_of_squarefree_of_isUnit_two_of_geometricallyConnected_tower_of_isUnit_three), and it cites [`CerednikDrinfeld.dvd_of_forall_frobenius_zpow_apply_eq_of_fixed`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.dvd_of_forall_frobenius_zpow_apply_eq_of_fixed).
